{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Now let the strength of HaShem grow.</b> The attribute of mercy prevails over the attribute of justice, to suppress Your anger — and this is the meaning of 'strength,' as it is written: ״טוב ארך אפיים מגבור״. Another interpretation: it refers to what was said above, that the nations would say, 'from inability' — therefore he said now, <b>now let the strength grow</b>, that is: show Your might to all, that You are able to bring them into the land and to cast down the kings before them." "<b>Strength of HaShem.</b> With alef, dalet (i.e., אדני)." "<b>As You spoke.</b> Regarding the incident of the calf. There is a discrepancy and variation here from what appears in the section of כי תשא. However, this is of no consequence, for such is the way of all Scripture: when the text changes its wording, it varies the second time from the first."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "He notes that כח here is read with the vowels of the divine name אדני."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:57.701746682Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}